.TH CHTTPCLIENT_RESP_HEADER_COUNT 3 "2026-09-29" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_resp_header_count \- count the lines of a response header
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

size_t chttpclient_resp_header_count(const chttpcli_response *resp,
                                     const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives the number of lines of the response header block
that carry the name that you give. The lookup ignores the case of the
name. Every such line counts once, whatever its value, and an empty
value counts too.

Use it with chttpclient_resp_header_at to read each occurrence of a
header that a server can send more than once, such as Set-Cookie.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
resp  The response to query. It can be NULL, and the function then
      gives 0.
name  The header name. It can be NULL, and the function then gives 0.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The number of lines with that name, or 0 if the response has none.
The function also gives 0 for a response from a streaming request,
which keeps no headers.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Only the header block of the response counts. A trailer field of a
chunked response body is not a response header, and it never counts
here.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
size_t n = chttpclient_resp_header_count(resp, "Set-Cookie");
for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++)
    printf("cookie: %s\\n",
           chttpclient_resp_header_at(resp, "Set-Cookie", i));
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_resp_header_at (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_header (3),
.BR chttpclient_resp_free (3)
